prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve, production candidate sprite sheet.
Create a new complete-character sprite sheet for DARKLIGHT REQUIEM, introducing ECLIPSE FANGS (Presas do Eclipse), supernatural martial arts gauntlets and greaves. Use the attached references as actual visual inputs.
REFERENCE ROLES: first image is the approved Requiem normal-form whole-character idle sheet, absolute authority for young face, large head/body proportions, brown wavy parted hair, black knee-length sleeved leather coat, black shirt/cargo trousers/belt/silver hip chain. Second is a complete sharp approved pixel-art character: only pixel-cluster rendering quality/proportions; DO NOT copy its daggers, purple crystals or purple hair into this NORMAL form. Third is the user's metal gauntlet/greave screenshot, equipment inspiration only, not that character/camera/style. Fourth is eye reference, same dark clearly RED irises (#C40814 with #5A0000 shadows), clean warm skin #F6AE82 base, no red makeup, no facial stripes, no under-eye stain.
Replace the HELD WEAPONS completely in these newly drawn frames with BOTH heavy fitted forearm gauntlets and BOTH knee-to-foot armored greaves. Fists fully enclosed. Original design: blackened steel, antique silver beveled edges, two curved fang ridges on each gauntlet, crescent-shaped knuckle plate, a recessed eclipse sigil on the forearm, matching tapered shin plates and armored boot toe. No literal animal heads. No swords, daggers, scythe, flails, chains held as weapons. Keep the small decorative silver hip chain from the approved costume. Keep coat, shirt, pants and face.
NORMAL-form aura: restrained dark crimson ember energy clinging to fists/forearms/shins/feet, brighter at strikes, localized pointed energy wedges and compact shock bursts rather than a body-obscuring cloud. Weapon stays metallic and recognizable.
MATCH THE EXISTING RPG GAME CAMERA: front and slightly elevated 2D RPG sprite camera, head and boots visible, compact youthful proportions like references, do not switch to realistic adult proportions, side-scrolling fighting-game or isometric perspective. Body anatomically same size across poses.
DRAW EXACTLY 12 entire separate characters in 3 rows of 4, read left to right, generous fully transparent gaps. Every head, coat, hand, foot, gauntlet, greave and effect must fit its own region. No text, labels, grid, panels, ground, cast shadow, checkerboard or watermark. Real transparent RGBA background. Crisp deliberate square pixel clusters, dark contour, restrained ramps, no blur/airbrush, no photorealism, same quality as the approved separate sprite.
FRAME PLAN:
0 relaxed low fighting guard, facing southeast three-quarter toward viewer, fists near ribs, feet planted, equipment clearly visible;
1 distinct breathing fighting guard same southeast direction, slight elbow and coat movement, same boot contact;
2 punch anticipation: right fist drawn back and left guard raised, weight on rear leg, SE;
3 explosive straight right punch extended toward lower right, torso rotates, left fist guarding, compact crimson knuckle impact, SE;
4 recovery into left knee chamber ready to kick, hands guarding, SE;
5 powerful extended left sidekick toward lower right, grounded right boot, readable full boot armor and crimson heel streak, SE;
6 spinning roundhouse kick: rear-three-quarter torso during true turn, one leg extended, whole head and both arms/legs visible, short crimson crescent trail;
7 crouched uppercut anticipation with both boots grounded, right fist low, SE;
8 launching rising right uppercut in the air, one knee lifted, full character airborne, compact rising crimson trail, SE;
9 airborne downward axe kick, one armored foot high and one striking diagonally down, fists guarding, body complete, SE;
10 powerful landing double-fist ground slam, wide crouch, small compact crimson impact burst, head upright visible, entire silhouette intact;
11 balanced recovery to same fighting guard as 0, different drawing settling coat, both boots grounded, aura fades.
This is one candidate preview sheet, not a finished Unity atlas. Prioritize readable distinct full-body martial poses and equipment consistency. All figures must be separated by transparent margins.
